Q: How to convert JSON response to List in C# RestSharp A: <p>It is not clear which json serializer/deserializer you are using, however try following steps</p>
<p>Using Newtonsoft</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>// Convert to JObject
JObject jsonObject = JObject.Parse(jsonResponse);
JArray eArr = JsonConvert.DeserializeObject&lt;JArray&gt;(jsonObject[&quot;data&quot;][&quot;emails&quot;]);


List&lt;string&gt; emails = eArr.Select(email =&gt; (string)email[&quot;value&quot;])
    .ToList();
</code></pre>
<p>You have not described <code>Job</code> class, but if <strong>Job</strong> class has property named <strong>Email</strong>, then</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>List&lt;Job&gt; jobList = eArr.Select(email =&gt; new Job(){Email = (string)email[&quot;value&quot;]} )
    .ToList();
</code></pre>
